# Gzip-compressed signed binaries staged for //go:embed (e.g. sideload host
# binaries like LogiAiPromptBuilder.exe.gz, per-stage <uuid>-T<technique>.exe.gz).
# These are produced by build_all.sh and cleaned at end of build; uploaded to
# PA out-of-band rather than committed (PE inside the gzip is signed).
*.exe.gz
*.dll.gz

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prebuilt-payload deployment tests: committed *input* binaries (allowlist)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These raw, UNSIGNED PEs are build INPUTS: build_all.sh signs them with the
# tenant cert, gzips them, and //go:embed's them at build time. Unlike the
# signed *.exe.gz artifacts above (regenerated per build), the raw payload must
# reach every git-synced tenant -- otherwise the build aborts at
# "Prebuilt payload <name> not found" (surfaced as a clamped "Command failed:
# bash .../build_all.sh" in the UI). The blanket *.exe rule (line 2) hides them,
# so each payload is re-included explicitly. Add ONE line per new prebuilt test.
#
# Keep entries < 50 MB. Larger payloads (e.g. e5472cd5 lab_assets/
# stage2_payload.exe, 66 MB) must NOT be committed here -- migrate those to
# git-LFS or keep them on the out-of-band Upload Binary path.
!tests_source/intel-driven/aa764293-94ed-4b25-a7fb-7d6fc14ac9a4/RoguePlanet.exe
# PENDING unsigned source: the only LogiAiPromptBuilder.exe copies on hand are
# F0RT1KA-signed (build_all.sh signs the sideload host in place). Drop the
# pristine unsigned vendor binary in place, verify with `osslsigncode verify`,
# then uncomment to commit:
# !tests_source/intel-driven/bf448c7a-307e-4458-ba36-341d6d8e671b/sideload_host/LogiAiPromptBuilder.exe

# Analysis outputs
analysis_output/

# .NET build outputs for embedded C# stages (e.g. HONESTCUE stage2_payload_src)
**/stage2_payload_src/bin/
**/stage2_payload_src/obj/
**/stage2_payload_src/publish/
